	abstract = {Governance rules about data are widely applied, but users cannot easily manage their compliance with such rules, especially in environments like large-scale data-intensive research, because of the complexity of dataﬂow and the time involved in understanding the rules. We believe the solution is to encode the rules in a computer actionable form, to allow machines to perform reasoning about them along with the dataﬂow. We intend that the encoded form is also easy to understand by humans. We discuss the challenges in the area, followed by our objectives and methodology in designing and using the rules to tackle the problem. Finally, we present our timetable for the proposal.},
